<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     FILE: Themes/Styles/AboutTypeScale.xaml
     PROJECT: ProGlassAutomation
     MODULE: About — the module type scale (size contract, not a colour)

     WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE, APP-LEVEL DICTIONARY
     ────────────────────────────────────────────
     2026-09-15 owner directive: "convert all cards and fonts safely move
     to dynamic so this about module can adapt the theme style."

     The About scale used to be declared inside
     Views/About/AboutIos26Theme.xaml — a dictionary merged LOCALLY by
     every About view. A locally declared key shadows Application.Resources,
     so nothing outside About could ever rewrite it: the module was frozen
     to one size ladder on every density profile.

     The scale is now declared once, at application level, where the
     density publisher (Services/Theme/AboutDensityTypeScale.cs, called
     from ThemeManager.PublishDensity) can rewrite it in place on every
     density switch. The values below are the COMPACT profile — the
     approved mockup scale and the app default — so the default rendering
     is unchanged; Normal / Comfortable / Spacious lift the sizes that are
     13 px or larger by 1–2 whole pixels.

     SNAPPING / WEIGHT RULES (unchanged, still enforced by the audit lock)
     ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Every size is a whole pixel and every size has a ROLE. The module
     used to hard-code 20 sizes, half of them fractional (13.5 / 12.5 /
     11.5 / 10.5); under TextOptions.TextFormattingMode="Display" a
     fractional size is hinted at a half-pixel grid, stems land between
     pixels, and the Bold / SemiBold cuts read muddy. Fractional sizes are
     banned outright.

     Weights reuse the ONE global scale (Weight.Regular / SemiBold / Bold
     from Themes/Styles/GlobalDesignSystem.xaml):
       • Weight.Regular   — body copy, muted field labels
       • Weight.SemiBold  — micro labels, chips, buttons, COMPACT (<= 13 px)
                            field values
       • Weight.Bold      — card / section titles, hero metrics, and field
                            VALUES at >= 14 px
     NEVER Weight.Bold below 12 px, and never Weight.SemiBold for a 17 px+
     title. AboutModuleAuditTests locks both rules.

     MDL2 glyph sizes reuse this same scale (a 16 px glyph is 16 px), so
     the module still has exactly ONE place where a font size is written
     down. Read a token as a size step, not as a text role, when it is
     applied to FontFamily.Icon.
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<ResourceDictionary
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Runtime">

    <sys:Double x:Key="Ios26FontSizeCaption">10</sys:Double>      <!-- micro kicker / footer note -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="Ios26FontSizeLabel">11</sys:Double>        <!-- small label -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="Ios26FontSizeSmall">12</sys:Double>        <!-- secondary / meta text -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="Ios26FontSizeBody">13</sys:Double>         <!-- body copy, field labels -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="Ios26FontSizeValue">14</sys:Double>        <!-- emphasised value -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="Ios26FontSizeSubtitle">15</sys:Double>     <!-- subtitle / large value -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="Ios26FontSizeCardTitleSm">16</sys:Double>  <!-- compact card title -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="Ios26FontSizeCardTitle">17</sys:Double>    <!-- card title -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="Ios26FontSizeSectionTitle">18</sys:Double> <!-- section title -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="Ios26FontSizeGlyph">19</sys:Double>        <!-- MDL2 glyph in a disc -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="Ios26FontSizeH2">20</sys:Double>           <!-- status headline -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="Ios26FontSizeH1">22</sys:Double>           <!-- page title -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="Ios26FontSizeMetric">24</sys:Double>       <!-- big number -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="Ios26FontSizeStat">28</sys:Double>         <!-- principle / stat number -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="Ios26FontSizeDisplay">30</sys:Double>      <!-- hero app name -->
</ResourceDictionary>
